<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CST, boxed beef generally lower on fairly good demand and moderate to heavy offerings.  Select and Choice chuck, round and loin cuts lower, while the rib cuts generally steady. Beef trimmings generally steady on light demand and offerings.-USDA</p>
<p> 327 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>  18 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>17 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     100.17	 98.70	 95.24	 93.78</p>
<p>Change	   -0.94	 -0.90	 -0.03	 -0.81</p>
<p>Rib	  149.29	146.32	140.61	139.22</p>
<p>Chuck	 73.44	 71.60	 75.94	 71.33</p>
<p>Round	 88.63	 88.63	 87.66	 87.66</p>
<p>Loin	 151.85	149.05	130.76	131.02</p>
<p>Brisket     72.39	 72.39	 71.53	 71.53</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  60.08	 60.01	 60.29	 60.15</p>
<p>Flank	 56.51	 56.51	 56.80	 56.80</p>
